  "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16{x}^{2}+55x+19}{(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n16{x}^{2}+55x+19=A(x+5)(x+1)+B(2x+1)(x+1)+C(2x+1)(x+5).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+55(-\\frac{1}{2})+19 & =A(-\\frac{1}{2}+5)(-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & +B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}+5) \\\\ 4-\\frac{55}{2}+19 & =A(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{46-55}{2} & =A(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ A & =\\frac{-36}{18} \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16(-5)^{2}+55(-5)+19 & =A(-5+5)(-5+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-5)+1)(-5+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-5)+1)(-5+5) \\\\ 400-275+19 & =B((-9)(-4)) \\\\ B & =\\frac{144}{36} \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16(-1)^{2}+55(-1)+19 & =A(-1+5)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-1)+1)(-1+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-1)+1)(-1+5) \\\\ 16-55+19 & =C(-4) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-20}{-4} \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{16{x}^{2}+55x+19}{(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)}=-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{4}{(x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x+1)}.\n$$",
